  <span data-pagefind-meta="title:Fertility Awareness-Based Methods Compared" style="display:none"></span>

  <p class="pillar-lead"><strong>Fertility awareness-based methods (FABMs) are ways to track your body's daily signals to know when you are and are not fertile. This guide compares seven: Standard Days, TwoDay, Billings, Creighton, the Sympto-Thermal Method, Marquette, and FEMM. Used carefully with a trained teacher, the best methods mean fewer than 2 in 100 women get pregnant in a year. Everyday-use numbers are higher, and no single method is best for everyone.</strong></p>

