    />
    <figcaption>The seven methods at a glance. Perfect-use figures are pregnancies per 100 women per year and are not directly comparable across studies. Full numbers and citations are in the table below.</figcaption>
  </figure>

<section id="comparison-table">
<h2>How the Methods Compare at a Glance</h2>

<p>The numbers below come from studies that used different designs and different ways of counting pregnancies. You cannot compare them straight across. All the research behind them is low to moderate quality. No method is ranked as better than another.</p>
